# Controls what ends up in GitHub's auto-generated archives:
#   - "Download ZIP" on the repo page
#   - https://codeload.github.com/<owner>/<repo>/zip/refs/heads/<branch>
#   - the source zip/tar.gz GitHub attaches to Releases
#
# GitHub builds all of these with `git archive` under the hood, which honors
# the export-ignore attribute below. A `git clone` (and this working tree)
# is unaffected -- export-ignore only strips paths from the generated
# archive, never from history or from anyone who clones normally.
#
# Net effect: the ZIP download is just the docs, README and LICENSE.
# Everything used to build/refresh the docs stays in the repo and in git
# history, it's just not bundled into the convenience download.

/update-docs.py             export-ignore
/DONTREADWHOLEFILE-llms-full.txt export-ignore
/.github/                   export-ignore
/.gitattributes             export-ignore
